252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #No, the previous mapping had several inaccuracies for the actual VIC-20 keyboard matrix.
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Key issues included:
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- Wrong row for F5 (it belongs in row 7, not mixed in).
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- Incorrect or missing assignments for the Commodore (C=) key.
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- Some symbol keys were assigned to the wrong matrix positions (e.g. * , + , = , 0, 2, 4, 6, 8).
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- The left arrow (←) is at row 1 col 7 (some tables also list it at row 6 col 7, but emulators
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #typically use row 1 col 7 for the physical key).
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- Row 7 was incomplete and had incorrect keys.
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #- A few Mac key codes were not the most practical matches for the VIC-20 layout.
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #The correct standard VIC-20 8x8 matrix positions (used by emulators like VICE) are:
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 0: DEL, 3, 5, 7, 9, +, £, 1
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 1: RETURN, W, R, Y, I, P, *, ←
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 2: ↓, A, D, G, J, L, ;, CTRL
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 3: F7, Z, C, B, M, ., R SHIFT, STOP
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 4: SPACE, S, F, H, K, :, =, →
252d68cc [grok-build-0.1] #Row 5: F1, E, T, U, O, @, ↑, Q
252d68cd [grok-build-0.1] #Row 6: F3, L SHIFT, X, V, N, ,, /, ← (per some tables)
252d68cd [grok-build-0.1] #Row 7: F5, C=, (mostly unused)
252d68cd [grok-build-0.1] #
252d68cd [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like me to provide the corrected mapping array and the update function using
252d68cd [grok-build-0.1] #CGEventSourceKeyState?
