262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.005 654B 5.92s
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The Commodore PET keyboard operates on the same fundamental matrix scanning principle as the VIC-20
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and C64, but there are a few key differences in the hardware implementation and matrix dimensions:
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Matrix Dimensions (10 × 8 vs. 8 × 8)
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• VIC-20 & C64: Both use an 8-row by 8-column matrix (64 distinct switch points).
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• PET: Uses a 10-row by 8-column matrix (80 possible switch points).
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Hardware Interface
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• VIC-20 / C64: Directly drive 8 output lines and read 8 input lines using two 8-bit
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #parallel ports (via the 6522 VIAs on VIC-20 or 6526 CIAs on C64).
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• PET: Uses a 74145 BCD-to-Decimal Decoder connected to PIA 1 (6520). The CPU
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #outputs a 4-bit binary value (0–9) to select one of the 10 rows (active low), and reads the 8
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #return lines via the other PIA port.
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Multiple Keyboard Variants
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Unlike the relatively uniform physical layouts of the VIC-20 and C64, the PET family has two
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #distinct layouts with completely different matrix mappings:
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Graphics Keyboard (Chiclet & Full-Travel):
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Found on the original PET 2001 and educational models (e.g., 4016/4032).
262ca908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Features dedicated numeric/cursor pads and graphic symbols printed directly on keys.
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Business Keyboard:
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Introduced with the PET 2001-N / 3000 / 8000 series.
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Resembles a standard typewriter layout with punctuation shifted, dedicated lowercase support,
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and lacks the PETSCII graphics on keytops.
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Requires a different matrix table and corresponding ROM (Editor ROM).
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Summary for Simulator Implementation
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you extend your current matrix implementation to accommodate a 10×8 grid and route the row
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #selection through a 4-bit input rather than a direct 8-bit bitmask, you will be able to reuse most
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #of your existing matrix polling logic. You will also want to support switching keymaps depending on
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #whether the system is configured as a Graphics or Business PET.
262ca909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
