262d82c7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.007 20.89KB 3.28s
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #On the Commodore PET, the 6520 PIA 1 handles keyboard scanning via two registers at address
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #range `E810`–`E813`:
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Row Selection (Output)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Address: `$E810` (PIA 1 Port A — `PRA`)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bits: Bits 0–3 (`PA0`–`PA3`)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Function: These 4 bits are connected to a 74145 BCD-to-Decimal Decoder, which
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #pulls one of the 10 matrix rows (0–9) LOW (`0`).
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Value: Values `0x0` through `0x9` select Row 0 through Row 9. Values `0xA`–`0xF` deselect
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #all rows.
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Column Selection / Input (Read)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Address: `$E812` (PIA 1 Port B — `PRB`)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bits: Bits 0–7 (`PB0`–`PB7`)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Function: The matrix columns are connected directly to Port B inputs with pull-up
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #resistors.
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Logic:
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `1` = Key is open / released
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `0` = Key is pressed (pulls line to ground)
262d82c8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
