262eeb81 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.061 209.1KB 7.77s
262eeb81 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The overall multi-system architecture is well-structured and covers a broad range of platforms
262eeb81 [gemini-3.7-flash] #(Commodore PET/VIC-20/C64/TED, Apple II, Atari DVG, and Ben Eater 6502 breadboard kit).
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #A few key observations and potential considerations across the shared files:
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. `macosffi.ts` — Keyboard Matrix Sentinel Check
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• In `readPetKeyboard()`, the check `if (key)` will evaluate to `false` for `kVK_ANSI_A` (`0x00`).
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• If `0` remains the placeholder for unassigned matrix slots, pressing the physical A key
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #will not register. Defining a sentinel constant (e.g., `-1`) for empty matrix cells and checking
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`if (key >= 0)` avoids this collision.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. `macosaudio.ts` — AudioQueue Buffer Recycling
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• In `playAudio()`, new native buffers are allocated via `AudioQueueAllocateBuffer` on every call
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and held indefinitely in `audioBuffers`.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• For long emulation runs, this can lead to memory growth. Utilizing the `noOpCallback` (which is
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #called when macOS completes playback of an enqueued buffer) to reclaim or reuse a fixed ring of
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #buffers (typically 2 to 4 buffers) would provide steady streaming without unbounded allocations.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. `machine.ts` — PET PIA Hardware Interaction
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The PIA 1 Port A write routing in `writePET()` now accounts for `CRA` Bit 2 before passing the
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #row index to `scanKeyboard()`.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Reading `E812` (`PIA1_PB`) properly clears the interrupt flags on `E813` (`CB1`/`CB2`) and
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #queries the active matrix state via `readPetMatrix()`.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The newly integrated opcodes (`1E` for `ASL abs,X` and `5E` for `LSR abs,X`) correctly handle
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #read-modify-write addressing through `targetAbsoluteX`.
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262eeb82 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you would like to refine any specific subsystem (such as buffer cycling in AudioQueue, the full
262eeb83 [gemini-3.7-flash] #PET Business/Graphics matrix array, or VIA/CIA timer interrupts), let me know.
262eeb83 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
