26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 deepseek-v4-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.027 72.94KB 100.55s
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #Thanks for sharing — this is new to me, and I had a quick look through the repo. It’s a compact
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #design: a cross-platform `terminal.ts` facade with split FFI/audio/MIDI modules, plus a
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #Unicode-width layer built around `Intl.Segmenter`.
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #A few things stood out:
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `stringwidth.ts` appears to contain two `export function stringWidth` declarations — one near the
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #top and one near the bottom. That’s likely to fail Deno’s type-checking as a duplicate function
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #implementation. There’s also a stray `Intl.localesargument` expression right after the header
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #comment.
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `windowsmidi.ts`: `closeMidi()` uses `for...in` over `Object.values(...)` for the output handles.
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #That iterates array indices, not the stored pointer values. The input loop uses `for...of`, so the
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #output loop looks like a typo.
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `macosmidi.ts`: `closeMidi()` is empty and `pollMidi()` always returns `[]`. The callback
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #plumbing exists, but the macOS MIDI input path doesn’t appear complete yet.
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689fe [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `joytest.ts`: the main `while` loop has no `sleep`, so it will busy-spin and print constantly.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #The other tests use a delay, so this one looks inconsistent.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `windowsffi.ts`: the PET key mapping contains values above 255, e.g. `49 + 256`, but
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #`GetAsyncKeyState` expects a virtual-key code only. Shifted entries need explicit modifier handling
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #instead.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `terminal.ts`: the `KeyBits` enum is 0-based while the actual bit constants in the same file are
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #powers of two. That’s easy to trip over, especially in a module with so many bit-oriented
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #functions.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #- `windowsaudio.ts`: `closeAudio()` calls `waveOutClose` directly without `waveOutReset` or
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #unwinding prepared headers. That can leave audio playing or leak WAVEHDRs during repeated use.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #The Unicode width work looks solid, especially the ZWJ handling and the Segmenter-based iteration.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #I’m happy to dig into any specific module further or help prepare fixes if that would be useful.
26e689ff [deepseek-v4-flash] #
